# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
# Board layer: Waveshare ESP32-P4-Module-DEV-KIT (ESP32-P4-Module + on-board C6).
# Layered LAST (see CMakeLists.txt) so it overrides nn-app-media's shared
# sdkconfig.defaults[.esp32p4], which is tuned for the ESP32-P4-WIFI6 board.
#
# Everything else — camera (IMX708 2304x1296 -> DIG-CROP 1920x1296), esp-hosted
# SDIO on the FUNC_BOARD pin set, 16 MB flash, partition table — is IDENTICAL to
# that board and is inherited unchanged.  Only the SILICON differs.

# ── Pre-3.0 silicon ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This kit's module is revision v1.3 (esptool: "ESP32-P4 (revision v1.3)"; its
# factory image reports "Min chip rev v0.1 / Max chip rev v1.99"), whereas the
# ESP32-P4-WIFI6 board is production v3.1.  The shared defaults deliberately
# leave ESP32P4_SELECTS_REV_LESS_V3 UNSET for that v3.1 part; here it must be
# set, otherwise the image is built rev-min v3.01 and this chip refuses it
# ("requires chip revision in range [v3.01 - v3.99]").
CONFIG_ESP32P4_SELECTS_REV_LESS_V3=y
CONFIG_ESP32P4_REV_MIN_100=y

# ── PSRAM speed follows from the revision ───────────────────────────────────
# SPIRAM_SPEED_250M is `depends on !ESP32P4_SELECTS_REV_LESS_V3`, so the shared
# defaults' 250M becomes unselectable the moment the flag above is set.  State
# 200M explicitly instead of relying on the silent fallback — and it matches the
# hardware, which enumerates at exactly that: the boot log reads
#   hex_psram: density 0x07 (256 Mbit), BitMode 0x01 (X16 Mode)
#   esp_psram: Found 32MB PSRAM device / Speed: 200MHz
CONFIG_SPIRAM_SPEED_200M=y

# ── esp-hosted buffers MUST live in PSRAM on this board ─────────────────────
# nn-app-media's shared defaults deliberately keep esp-hosted's tasks and mempool
# in INTERNAL RAM (cache-safe stacks).  That fits on the v3.1 WIFI6 board but NOT
# here: esp-hosted's init runs before the scheduler and consumed ~437 KB of
# internal RAM, so FreeRTOS then could not allocate the 1536-byte IDLE task stack
# and the board reboot-looped on
#     assert failed: vApplicationGetIdleTaskMemory port_common.c:53
# Instrumenting that allocation showed the smoking gun — internal exhausted while
# PSRAM sat empty:
#     idle alloc fail: want=1536 int_free=3056 int_big=1152 spi_free=33550924
# Moving esp-hosted to PSRAM restores a healthy split (internal=446 KB free).
# NOTE the mechanism is only partly understood: the likely reason the same
# settings fit on v3.1 is that SPIRAM_ALLOW_STACK_EXTERNAL_MEMORY can place task
# stacks in PSRAM there, whereas this pre-3.0 part keeps them internal — so these
# two options just make explicit what v3.1 does implicitly.  If SDIO throughput
# ever looks poor on this board, suspect these first.
CONFIG_ESP_HOSTED_DFLT_TASK_FROM_SPIRAM=y
CONFIG_ESP_HOSTED_MEMPOOL_PREFER_SPIRAM=y

# ── Known v1.3 silicon limitations (informational, no action) ───────────────
# * ISP black-level correction is unavailable:
#     ISP_BLC: BLC is not supported on ESP32P4 chips prior than v3.0
#   esp_video logs "BLC configure failed — continuing without" and carries on.
# * CPU tops out at 360 MHz (v3.x parts reach 400 MHz) — IDF derives this.
# * The on-board C6 reports esp-hosted slave version 0.0.0 against our 2.12.x
#   host ("Version mismatch ... Upgrade co-proc to avoid RPC timeouts").  The
#   link negotiates and works; if RPC timeouts appear, reflash the C6 slave.

# ── Wide NoIR colour: WB gains are the LIVE colour control ──────────────────
# nn_camera_set_wb() builds the ISP CCM as CCM_BASE x per-channel WB gains and
# that matrix is what the image actually gets — measured 2026-08-02: sweeping
# the IPA JSON's acc.ccm (row scale x0.82, then sum-preserving R->G shifts up
# to 25%) moved R/G by <1%, so on this firmware the JSON ccm is inert and the
# Kconfig gains below are authoritative.  The shared default (R=B=1620 milli,
# "variant F", tuned on the IR-cut camera) over-reds the NoIR: no IR-cut filter
# means IR lands in the red channel on top of the 1.62x gain -> measured
# R/G=1.46, B/G=1.20.  Values below target neutral (~1.0) on the same scene.
# Re-trimmed 2026-08-03 after nn_camera began disabling the ISP's WB BLOCK (the
# purple-band culprit — see nn_camera.c capture_task).  That block had been
# attenuating R/B underneath these gains, so the old values (1280/1600) over-
# corrected once it was off (measured R/G 1.50, B/G 1.74).  Live-trimmed via
# `isp wb` back to the user-validated warm-neutral (R/G=B/G≈1.05-1.11).
CONFIG_NN_CAMERA_WB_R_MILLI=1001
CONFIG_NN_CAMERA_WB_B_MILLI=1110
